course: dictionary
lesson: 8335
title: Words about people and their language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a group of people, and some name the language they speak. Romani is one of these. It can be a noun for the people, a noun for their language, or an adjective that describes something as belonging to them. The words around it show which one it is.
explain: «Flamenco comes from Andalusia in southern Spain, with Romani roots, and uses guitar, singing, clapping and fast, strong footwork.» The words «with Romani roots» tell you where the dance began, so here Romani describes the roots. It is an adjective.
explain: Context also tells you how people feel about a word. Some people prefer «Romani people» to the older word «gypsy», which some see as rude. When you are not sure how a word is used, look at how others use it, and ask a trusted adult.
fact: Romani can be a noun: the Romani people, or the Romani language.
fact: Romani can be an adjective, as in «Romani music».
fact: The Romani people's ancestors came from India about a thousand years ago.
fact: Romani is a language related to languages of India, and it is also spelt Romany.
fact: «Flamenco» has Romani roots and can show proud, angry or sad feelings, not only happy ones.
exercise: «Flamenco comes from Andalusia in southern Spain, with Romani roots.» In this sentence, what kind of word is Romani? | *An adjective, describing the roots | A noun for a town | A name for a country | A verb for dancing
exercise: Romani is a language related to languages of which country? | Italy | *India | Egypt | Spain
exercise: Some people see the word «gypsy» as rude. Which is a respectful choice? | *Romani people | Gypsy, always, to be funny | Gypsy folk, as a joke | Strangers from far away
test: Which phrase uses Romani as an adjective? | Romani is hard to learn | *Romani music | The Romani came from India | Speak Romani
test: About how long ago did the Romani ancestors come from India? | *About a thousand years ago | Ten years ago | Yesterday | Last year
exam: Which statement about Romani is true? | It is a type of guitar | *It can be a noun for a people, a noun for a language, or an adjective | It is always a noun for a dance | It means only Spanish
